Ex) Rule 21 (primitive type variable should not be zero)
    {v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≠ 0

[Example Rules]
Rule 10 (valid 2D transposed convolution)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int, v_4 : int} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 4 ∧ v_3 ≥ 1 ∧ v_4 ≥ 0 ∧ v_3 × (shape(v_1, 2) − 1) + shape(v_2, 2) − 2 × v_4 > 0 ∧ v_3 × (shape(v_1, 3) − 1) + shape(v_2, 3) − 2 × v_4 > 0

Rule 3 (input tensors must have the same number of dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)

Rule 11 (index tensor (v_3) is within the input tensor along the specified dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= min(v_3) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_3) ≤ shape(v_1, v_2) − 1

Rule 12 (a primitive type variable is smaller than the other)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float, v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≤ v_2

Rule 14 (tensor should not be empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) − 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0

